        root cause: The function cJSON_Minify reads past the end of the input buffer in two cases: (1) when a multiline comment is unterminated, the loop exits at the null terminator but then `json += 2` advances two bytes past it; (2) when a string literal is unterminated, the loop exits at the null terminator but the code unconditionally copies that null terminator and increments `json` one byte past it. Both cause the outer `while (*json)` loop to read out of bounds.
