Root cause: The string literal parsing loop reads one byte past the allocated buffer when the string ends with a backslash followed by the null terminator, because it unconditionally copies the character after a backslash without checking for the null terminator.
Fix: In the string parsing loop, after copying a backslash, check if the next character is the null terminator; if so, break out of the loop instead of copying it. Also restructure the loop to avoid the unconditional second copy.

